So I'm playing a gnomish wizard and having fun using the endless power
regen and hungerless casting to create and destroy hoardes of
monsters. I've toyed with the idea of an extinctionist game for years,
but have never had the patience; this time will probably be similar,
but I'd like to keep going as long as I can.

I've killed at least two dozen unicorns so far, and despite carefully
arranging them in groups of four and polypiling endlessly (along with
many other tools, magical and non), have only managed to produce a
single magic marker. I already wasted half the charges on one and
nearly used up another just to write the stupid polymorph spellbook in
the first place, as past turn 80,000 I have yet to find any book,
wand, or potion of polymorph in the main dungeon. I have more scrolls
than I can shake a stick at and am itching to write more enchant armor
(which has been very scarce) and charging (ring of increase damage is
edible this game); yes I've polypiled scrolls too of course. I'm
wondering how much longer I should keep at it before giving up and
diving into Gehennom, or blowing another wish (my wand of wishing is
currently 1:3 and my ascension kit is complete except for a ring of
free action).

I also tamed an angel and an archon, actually two of the latter but
one was eaten by a trapper. I noticed that angels can wear body armor
even though archons can't, so I made the angel a black dragon scale
mail. He put it on, but then I realized that red would be a more
useful color, as his shield already reflects disintegration rays, and
he's not fire resistant so probably won't last long otherwise once I
go below the Valley. (I could give him Firebrand to wield, but I'm
afraid he'll destroy too many useful scrolls and potions.) If I made
red scale mail and enchanted it higher than the +1 black scale mail
he's currently wearing, do you think he would switch armor on his own?
Same with speed boots? (He's already wearing my old +6 elven helm.) Or
should I just forget about him and tame another archon? I gave the
angel +6 Demonbane but he won't drink potions of gain level so has far
fewer hit points than my surviving archon (who has Sunsword). I do
have a bullwhip so can relieve them both of their weapons easily at
least.

